# Optimized Pharmacy Invoice Import

We have successfully enhanced the AyurStock Pro "Import Bill" feature to automatically handle purchase invoices with batch numbers, expiry dates, and quantities.

## Key Enhancements

### 1. Robust AI Parsing
We updated the `SYSTEM_PROMPT` in [aiParser.ts](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/lib/aiParser.ts) to explicitly recognize the structure of pharmacy invoices. The AI now extracts:
- **Batch Numbers**
- **Expiry Dates** (e.g., "Jan-28")
- **Quantities** (as requested for your 7-medicine invoice)
- **Purchase Rates** (PTS)

### 2. Enhanced Preview UI
The "Import Bill" preview table in [import-price-list.tsx](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/components/medicine/import-price-list.tsx) now includes a **Qty** column, allowing you to review and adjust the extracted quantities before they are added to your stock.

### 3. Smart Inventory Integration
The backend import API in [bulk-import/route.ts](file:///c:/Users/vaibh/Documents/Ayur-stock%20pro/app/api/medicine/bulk-import/route.ts) has been significantly upgraded. Instead of just adding medicines to your "Master" list, it now:
- **Automatically creates Inventory Batches** for each medicine if batch and quantity data is available.
- **Parses Expiry Dates** accurately (handling formats like "MMM-YY").
- **Accumulates Stock** if the same batch is imported multiple times.

### 4. Safety & Isolated Changes
> [!IMPORTANT]
> As per your request, these changes are isolated to the **"Import Bill"** (Inventory) flow. The regular **"Import Medicines"** (Medicine Master PDF) feature remains unchanged and will continue to work exactly as it did before.

